{title: 045 - Open Now Thy Gates of Beauty}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #045 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 45}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm/D]Open [Dm/F]now [Gm]thy [Cm/G]gates [Bb]of beauty,
[Bb]Zion, let [Adim]me enter [Bb]there,
[Bb/D]Where my soul in [Gm]joyful [F]duty
[Bb]Waits for God [Dm/A]Who [Bb]answers [Adim]prayer.
[Bb]Oh, how [Adim]bless'd is [Bb]this [Gm]place,
[Bb]Filled with [Dm/A]solace, [Cm/G]light, [F]and [Bb/F]grace!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm/D]Gracious [Bb/F]God, [Gm]I [F]come [Bb]before [Dm/A]Thee,
[Bb]Come Thou also [Adim]unto [Bb]me;
[Bb/D]Where we find Thee [Gm]and [Cm/G]adore [F/A]Thee,
[Bb]There a heav'n [Dm/A]on [Bb]earth must [Adim]be.
[Bb]To my [Adim]heart, oh, [Bb]enter [Adim]Thou,
[Bb]Let it [Dm/A]be [Gm]Thy [Cm/G]temple [Bb/F]now!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm/D]Here [Dm]Thy [Bb/F]praise [Gm]is [F]gladly [Bb]chanted,
[Bb]Here Thy seed [Adim]is duly [Bb]sown;
[Bb/D]Let my soul, where [Gm]it [Cm/G]is [F]planted,
[Bb]Bring forth precious sheaves [Adim]alone,
[Bb]So that [Adim]all I [Bb]hear [Gm]may [Adim]be
[Bb]Fruitful [Dm/A]unto [Cm/G]life [F]in [Bb/F]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm/D]Thou [Dm]my [Bb/F]faith [Gm]increase [Bb]and quicken,
[Bb]Let me keep [Adim]Thy gift [Bb]divine,
[Bb/D]Howsoe'er temptations [Cm/G]thicken;
[Bb]May Thy Word [Dm/A]still [Bb]o'er me [Adim]shine
[Bb]As my [Adim]guiding [Bb]star [Gm]through [Adim]life,
[Bb]As my [Dm/A]comfort [Cm/G]in [F]my [Bb/F]strife.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Gm/D]Speak, [Dm]O [Bb/F]God, [Gm]and [F]I [Bb]will hear [Dm/A]Thee,
[Bb]Let Thy [Adim]will be [Bb]done indeed;
[Bb/D]May I undisturbed [Cm/G]draw [F]near Thee
[Bb]While Thou [Dm/A]dost [Bb]Thy people feed.
[Bb]Here of [Adim]life the [Bb]fountain [Adim]flows;
[Bb]Here is [Dm/A]balm [Gm]for [Cm/G]all [F]our [Bb/F]woes.
{end_of_verse}
